        '3) Ovulation phase: Rising estrogen triggers the pituitary to release luteinizing hormone (LH), prompting the ovary to release a mature egg down the fallopian tube. In a 28-day cycle, this happens around day 14 and lasts about 24 hours. Notable signs include a slight rise in basal body temperature and stretchy cervical discharge resembling egg whites. Keep in mind that sperm can live up to 5 days in fertile cervical fluid, meaning intercourse up to 5 days before ovulation can result in pregnancy.',
